1 NOTE Born 24 Nov 1883 in Glasgow (1918 naturalization; the 1921 passport says 24 Dec). Iron worker. Sailed from Glasgow on the Allan Line ship Numidian on 6 Jul 1911, bound for Boston. Naturalized in 1918 and 1920; carpenter; lived in Jamaica Plain. His 1921 passport application lists his wife Magdalene and son Alexander, born in Glasgow, and his father Alexander McLellan, born in Scotland and deceased. Died 1952; buried at Saint Joseph Cemetery, West Roxbury. His wife's 1953 obituary names their sons Alexander and Gordon Jr.
